#include "fl_agent_internal.h"

/* Sections of the manual; each stays below the portable string literal limit. */
const char *const FL_AGENT_REFERENCE[] = {
"# Flow authoring reference\n"
"\n"
"Flow is a motion-graphics and video editor. A project holds scenes; a scene is a canvas (default 1920x1080) holding\n"
"entities (shapes, text, images) arranged in a hierarchy, a timeline of beats, keyframe animation, audio clips and\n"
"optional Lua scripts. Everything is edited with `apply_ops`: atomic, undoable batches of typed operations.\n"
"\n",
"## Native composition and behavior ownership\n"
"Script schema8 stores ordinary Lua asset references, typed bindings, layer, parameters, time and build overrides.\n"
"outputs={self={x='replace'},target={y='add'}} declares numeric replace/add/multiply or text replacement; reads={target={x=true}} exposes evaluated ctx.inputs.target from strictly lower layers. ctx.bindings remains native input.\n"
"scope.edit {entity:owner,component:generator,target:localEntity,path?:[localGeneratorIds],value:editOrArray} edits generated native content. Edits: entity.add/patch/remove, component.set/patch/remove, timeline.patch {duration?,beats?,clips?}. Component ID0 allocates a reserved extension ID. prototype.detach {entity} preserves an owned scope with clocks and behaviors.\n"
"bake_scene {action:'start',scene,start,end,step,tolerance} captures native data asynchronously; poll/status/cancel/apply with returned token. Times are seconds. Apply rejects a changed project and is undoable. Tolerance is checked at captured ticks; nested clocks/media are preserved.\n"
"Native events component version1 has events={next_id,points:[{id,at,name,value}]}. ctx.events delivers ordered step inputs and time-zero initialize events; sample receives no events.\n"
"Native properties also include radius, blur, gradient_angle, shadow_blur/x/y, gradient_to, shadow_color, media_time. Lua uses style fields and media.seconds; -1 follows video placement. Native angles use radians. evaluate_scene includes native properties and writer provenance.\n"
"\n",
"## Units and conventions\n"
"- Times and durations are SECONDS (decimals allowed). Rotation is DEGREES. Positions and sizes are scene pixels,\n"
"  local to the parent; the origin is the top-left corner of the canvas and y grows downward.\n"
"- Colours are \"#RRGGBB\" or \"#RRGGBBAA\" (or [r,g,b,a] with 0..255). Opacity is 0..1.\n"
"- Ids are positive integers, represented as decimal strings beyond 2^53. Inside one `apply_ops` batch, give a created object a name with `\"as\": \"$title\"` and use\n"
"  \"$title\" wherever an id is expected in later operations.\n"
"- Later entities in a scene draw on top of earlier ones. `entity.reorder` changes that order.\n"
"\n",
"## Workflow\n"
"1. `get_project` for scenes and assets, `get_scene` for one scene's full contents (use its `revision` in `expect`).\n"
"2. Build with `apply_ops`. Prefer one batch per logical change; a failing operation applies nothing and names the\n"
"   failing index. Use `dry_run: true` to validate a plan.\n"
"3. Check the result with `review_scene` (text: framing, type, overlap, contrast, motion, script errors). Call `render_frame` only for a contact sheet of a procedural background, a few times, and stop when it returns unchanged. `evaluate_scene` with sparse:true reports numbers.\n"
"4. `undo`/`redo` revert whole batches. GUI and MCP share the same history.\n"
"\n",
"## Scene time: beats\n"
"A scene's length is the sum of its beats; every scene starts with one 5 s beat. Beats are narrative steps. Keyframes\n"
"can anchor to a beat edge so they follow when the beat is retimed. Normalized beat positions stretch with `beat.update`; fixed offsets keep their units. Deletion leaves unbound\n"
"key/audio bindings inactive until rebound or undone. New keyframe times must lie within 0..scene length, so create or extend beats first.\n"
"\n",
"## Operations (`apply_ops` `ops` items)\n"
"scene.add {name} -> id\n"
"scene.remove {scene} | scene.rename {scene,name} | scene.move {scene,position}\n"
"scene.set {scene, width?, height?, aspect?: [w,h]|null, camera?: [x,y], background?: \"#RRGGBB\"}\n"
"entity.create {scene, kind, parent?, asset?, props?} -> id\n"
"  kind: entity, rectangle, ellipse, triangle, diamond, hexagon, star, line, arrow, text, image (image needs asset = an image asset id)\n"
"entity.set {entity, props}      entity.remove {entity} (removes the subtree)\n"
"entity.reparent {entity, parent|null}      entity.reorder {entity, position}\n"
"  props: name, visible, x, y, width, height, rotation, scale_x, scale_y, opacity,\n"
"         fill, stroke, stroke_width (shapes), text, font_size, font_family, font_weight, italic, align (text),\n"
"         asset (image, video), radius (rectangle, image, video), fill2 + gradient_angle (rectangle, ellipse, triangle, diamond, hexagon, star: two-colour gradient\n"
"         from fill to fill2; angle in degrees, 0 = left to right, 90 = top to bottom), shadow_blur, shadow_x, shadow_y,\n"
"         shadow_color (rectangle, ellipse, image, video), start, offset, rate, loop (video),\n"
"         crop: [x, y, width, height] fractions of the source an image or video shows (default [0,0,1,1]),\n"
"         clip (any entity: it and its children are cut to its box, rounded by radius; empty entities clip too), blur (any entity:\n"
"         gaussian blur in scene pixels of the entity together with its children, applied before clipping)\n"
"  Not every kind has every prop: empty entities have no fill; lines/arrows have a stroke but no fill; images and videos only an asset.\n"
"\n",
"  Stored x and y are the pivot. New shapes are created with the pivot at the box centre, and the x,y you pass to entity.create is still the visual top-left. Rotation and scale happen around the pivot. Text wraps at spaces inside its box. tracking, stagger, rise, text_fade and text_duration animate glyphs of one text entity. text_delay is the scene time when that entrance starts; set it to the current time to play the entrance again when the line changes. A path's fill paints the interior of a closed curve and its stroke paints the trimmed curve, so a transparent fill is a stroke-only draw-on. Path commands are local pixels (M, L, C) with trim_start and trim_end. Effect kinds 1..5 are built in (domain warp, blob, grain, fringe, displacement); kind 6 is custom GLSL function `vec4 effect(vec2 uv, float time, vec4 a, vec4 b)` with uniforms u0..u7. A custom effect may call pixelUv(), sceneColor(fragUv), cameraRay(fragUv), cameraOrigin(fragUv) and sceneDepth(world). sceneColor is the straight-alpha image of entities parented under the effect (white if it has none); those children are drawn into the shader instead of on top of it, so the shader can bend, hide and composite them. Blur on that effect blurs the child image before the shader reads it. cameraRay and cameraOrigin are the scene camera's ray through that pixel. sceneDepth(world) writes that camera's depth so meshes in front of the shader stay in front. mask is the same child image, premultiplied. Names flCam, pixelUv, sceneColor, cameraRay, cameraOrigin, sceneDepth and mask are provided. Blend is 0 normal, 1 add, 2 multiply, 3 screen. Camera grade is vignette, grain, lift, gamma and gain. An orthographic camera looks along its local -Z. Near and far are distances along that axis. Artwork at z = 0 is in frame when the camera sits about one picture-height in front of it.\n"
"  Video: kind video with asset = a video asset id. It plays from `start` (scene seconds, default 0) at source position\n"
"  `offset`, speed `rate`; before start it shows the first frame, after the end it holds the last (or loops).\n"
"  `set` changes BASE values. A property that has keyframes keeps following them; edit the keys instead.\n"
"key.set {entity, property, at, value, ease?, key?} -> key id\n"
"  property: x y width height rotation scale_x scale_y opacity fill stroke stroke_width font_size,\n"
"            crop_x crop_y crop_w crop_h (images/videos: animate to zoom and pan inside a fixed frame)\n"
"  at: seconds, or {\"beat\": id, \"edge\": \"start\"|\"end\", \"offset\": seconds}\n"
"  Or at: {\"beat\": id, \"position\": 0..1, \"offset\": seconds}; normalized position stretches, offset stays fixed.\n"
"  ease: linear (default), in, out, in_out, hold. The ease shapes the segment from this key to the next.\n"
"  Setting a key at the time of an existing key replaces it. Values between keys are interpolated.\n"
"key.remove {key}      track.remove {entity, property}\n"
"beat.add {scene, name, duration, position?, auto_advance?} -> id      beat.update {beat, name?, duration?, auto_advance?}\n"
"beat.remove {beat}    beat.move {beat, position}    beat.split {beat, at, name} -> id of the new right-hand beat\n"
"clip.add {scene, asset, start?, source_offset?, duration?, gain?, fade_in?, fade_out?} -> id   (asset must be audio;\n"
"  duration 0 or omitted plays to the end of the asset; gain 0..4)\n"
"clip.update {clip, ...same fields}      clip.remove {clip}\n"
,
"prototype.capture {entity, name} -> asset id     prototype.instantiate {scene, asset, parent?, x?, y?} -> owner entity id\n"
"prototype.overrides {entity, value: [{op, path: [nested component IDs], entity, component?, value?}]}\n"
"  Overrides: entity.patch/add/remove, component.patch/set/remove; extension IDs have the high bit set.\n"
"  Missing targets are retained as unresolved overrides. evaluate_scene includes generated entities and provenance.\n"
"asset.source {asset?, kind: lua|flproto, name?, source?} -> id (new assets require name and source)\n"
"asset.rename {asset, name}     asset.remove {asset} (requires removing all references first)\n"
"script.create {name, source} -> id     script.update {script, name?, source?, edits?: [{old, new}]}\n"
"  component.set {entity, value} (typed component JSON from get_scene.components; id=0 creates an instance)\n"
"  component.remove {entity, component} (stable component instance id; Transform is required)\n"
"  script.remove {script} (requires detaching all references first)     script.attach {entity, script, enabled?}     script.detach {entity}\n"
"  Scripts are project assets and are shared: attach one asset to any number of entities. Names are unique\n"
"  per project. Invalid syntax or attached declarations reject the whole batch. edits patch the\n"
"  text; every old must match exactly once. The set_script and get_script tools do the same without a batch.\n"
"\n",
"## Lua scripts\n"
"Create Lua assets (script.create / set_script), then attach them as repeatable Script components.\n"
"One returned module supports optional build(ctx), initialize(ctx), step(ctx), sample(ctx), parameters, typed bindings and step_hz.\n"
"build(ctx) returns a typed version-one flproto descriptor and runs on document changes, not every frame.\n"
"imports={alias=\"LuaAssetId\"} declares tracked Lua asset dependencies; callbacks/build use ctx.imports.alias.\n"
"Imports are fresh per callback, shared by diamond aliases within that callback, bounded and cycle-checked.\n"
"ctx.entity starts with keyframed entity values. Write pose.{x,y,z,rx,ry,rz,scale_x,scale_y,scale_z} (radians),\n"
"bounds.{width,height,depth}, camera, material, light, particles, post, appearance, opacity and crop.\n"
"appearance.{fill,stroke (RGBA arrays 0..255),stroke_width,font_size}, opacity, crop.{x,y,width,height}, or text (16 MiB aggregate frame budget).\n"
"ctx.time supplies local tick, seconds, duration, progress, cycle, phase and composition_seconds.\n"
"ctx.params merges instance overrides with module parameter defaults. Declarations support number/integer/boolean/\n"
"string/vec2/color with default, label, description and numeric min/max. Unknown names or invalid values fail sampling.\n"
"Declare bindings={target={type='entity'}} in Lua; set the Script bindings object to \"target\":{\"type\":\"entity\",\"id\":\"<id>\"}.\n"
"ctx.bindings contains native callback-time snapshots, never another behavior's sampled outputs. Types: entity, component, region, asset.\n"
"Component references additionally require entity. Missing referenced targets produce runtime diagnostics; optional=true permits omitted wiring.\n"
"component.set edits attachment parameters, bindings and time mapping using the same typed JSON as scene files. Whole-scene or\n"
"beat-bound clocks support stretch/fixed speed, looping and before/after hold; missing beats produce diagnostics.\n"
"Available: math, string, table, utf8, ipairs, pairs (stable order), select, tonumber, tostring, type, assert, error.\n"
"No files, network, os, require, pcall or coroutines. Randomness is deterministic per entity/component instance.\n"
"Limits: 1M instructions per sample and 16 MiB per evaluator. Errors keep keyframed values and appear as script_error.\n"
"Example: return {sample=function(ctx) ctx.entity.pose.y=ctx.entity.pose.y+math.sin(ctx.time.seconds*4)*20 end}\n"
"\n",
"## Assets\n"
"`import_asset {path}` copies a local image, audio, video, font or Lua file into the project and returns its id. Asset\n"
"imports use the shared undo history. Images are placed with entity.create kind=image.\n"
"\n",
"## Errors\n"
"Failures return {error:{code,message}}: invalid_argument, unknown_field, missing_field, unknown_reference, not_found,\n"
"not_applicable, rejected (the document refused the values), revision_conflict, conflict (undo/redo refused), no_project.\n", NULL};
